---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="BookSkim privacy policy"
  description="BookSkim has no accounts, no ads and no tracking. Your books and reading activity stay on your device."
>
  <section class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your data, your device</p>
      <h1 class="h2">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="doc__date">Last updated 5 July 2026</p>

      <div class="doc__body">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          There are no accounts, no ads and no tracking in BookSkim. Your books
          and everything about how you read them stay on your phone. We do not
          sell or share your data, because we do not collect it.
        </p>

        <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
        <p>Everything BookSkim creates is stored on your device only:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The EPUB files you import, and your library</li>
          <li>Reading progress, bookmarks, highlights and reading position</li>
          <li>Reading streaks, time read, and per-book settings</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          None of it is uploaded to us or to any server. Uninstall the app and
          it goes with it.
        </p>

        <h2>When the app uses the internet</h2>
        <p>Three times, and only when you ask:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Dictionary lookup.</strong> Tapping a word sends that word
            to a dictionary service to fetch a definition. The word is sent on
            its own. Not the sentence, not the page, not the book.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Web search.</strong> Tapping search opens your browser with
            the term you selected.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Bug reports.</strong> If you send one from Settings, it
            includes your device model and app version along with what you write.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Everything else works with the SIM out.</p>

        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <p>
          BookSkim asks for file access so you can pick EPUB files to import. It
          reads the files you choose and nothing else.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          BookSkim collects no personal information from anyone, of any age.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Material
          changes will be noted in the app's release notes.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about any of this:
          <a href="mailto:hello@wildkidstudio.in">hello@wildkidstudio.in</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc { padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); }
  .doc__date { color: var(--ink-faint); margin-top: 1rem; font-size: .95rem; }

  .doc__body { max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .doc__body h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: .75rem;
  }
  .doc__body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .doc__body p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .doc__body ul {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .doc__body li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .doc__body strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .doc__body a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
